From: dolf3131 <144650661+dolf3131@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:05:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Tool calls: a block ends where its call ends, so a
 </tool_call> inside an argument is text

vLLM's Qwen parser and veloGB10 0.7.4 (--tool-block-end after-function): a close ends the block only
after </function> or </parameter> (JSON body: }) and when it does not pay for a <tool_call> the block
itself opened; a finished reply falls back to the first close, a streaming one waits. Applied to the
end parser, the streamed content and the single-call filter. Complements the prompt-side escape,
which cannot cover a tag the model writes itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
